&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;(1) Assets recoverable without earning a return.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Our significant regulatory assets and liabilities include:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Difference between gas retained and gas consumed in operations. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts reflect the value of the difference between the quantity of gas retained for fuel and lost and unaccounted for (L&amp;amp;U) and the quantity of gas consumed and L&amp;amp;U experienced in our operations. Pursuant to our tariff, the quantities associated with these amounts are expected to be recovered from or returned to our customers in subsequent periods. On a periodic basis, we file reports with the FERC detailing our volumetric fuel and L&amp;amp;U reimbursement activity and establishing prospective fuel and L&amp;amp;U retention rates. Volumetric over- or under-collections of fuel and L&amp;amp;U quantities from prior periods are trued up through either an addition or reduction to the prospective fuel and L&amp;amp;U retention rates.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we recorded a net regulatory expense of $0.1 million and a net regulatory benefit of $0.2 million, respectively, related to our fuel and L&amp;amp;U activity.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Income tax related. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Amounts represent the anticipated return to ratepayers of deferred income taxes as a result of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017, which lowered the U.S. federal corporate income tax rate from 35% to 21% effective January 1, 2018. These amounts are amortized to Account 411.1 &amp;#8220;Provision for Deferred Income Taxes &amp;#8211; Credit&amp;#8221; over the remaining depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;7. Recent Accounting Pronouncement&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;ASU No. 2025-06&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On September 18, 2025, the Financial Accounting Standards Board issued ASU No. 2025-06, &amp;#8220;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-style: italic;"&gt;Intangibles&amp;#8212;Goodwill and Other&amp;#8212;Internal-Use Software (Subtopic 350-40): Targeted Improvements to the Accounting for Internal-Use Software.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#8221; This ASU modernizes the accounting guidance for the costs to develop software for internal use by removing outdated stage-based cost capitalization rules and replacing them with a probability-based cost-capitalization framework that aligns better with current software development methods. This ASU will be effective for annual periods beginning after December 15, 2027, for interim reporting periods beginning within those annual periods, and early adoption is permitted. Management is currently evaluating this ASU to determine its impact on the Company&amp;#8217;s financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
